## SECTION 8: BIDIRECTIONAL DUAL PAIRING
##
## Network operations are dual mirrors of multiuser operations.

MULTIUSER ⇄ NETWORK DUAL PAIRS:

⊙:register_user ⇄ ⊙:connect_peer (user registration ↔ peer connection)
⊙:authenticate_user ⇄ ⊙:send_message (user auth token ↔ message auth/integrity)
⊙:create_session ⇄ ⊙:receive_message (session creation ↔ message reception)
⊙:grant_permission ⇄ ⊙:replicate_state (grant access to resource ↔ replicate to peer)
⊙:verify_permission ⇄ ⊙:detect_version_divergence (check if user can access ↔ check if peer has different version)
⊙:broadcast_event ⇄ ⊙:rank_peer_versions (event to users ↔ version ranking across peers)
⊙:invite_to_collaboration ⇄ ⊙:await_peer_consensus (user invited ↔ peer consensus awaited)
⊙:accept_collaboration_invitation ⇄ ⊙:resolve_version_conflict (user accepts ↔ conflict resolved)
⊙:handle_concurrent_edits ⇄ ⊙:full_sync_with_peers (user edits merged ↔ full state synced)
⊙:sync_user_state ⇄ ⊙:watch_state_changes (user state synced ↔ peer state watched)
⊙:audit_multiuser_events ⇄ ⊙:audit_network_events (user audit ↔ network audit)
⊙:verify_ledger_integrity ⇄ ⊙:verify_replication_consistency (user ledger verified ↔ replication verified)

RESULT: 12 DUAL PAIRS CONFIRMED ✓

